{"schemaVersion":1,"sourcePath":"C:/Users/Lenovo/.pi/.pi/plans/2026-11-21-timeout-builder-recovery.md","digest":"3c07d834d86cdf5e135700c6027b74e0c2fe02140e16b14ed5414244f1e4877b","title":"Adaptive Command Recovery and Stall-Safe Builder Supervision","requirements":[{"roadmapStepId":"rm-1","label":"1","text":"**Rebaseline and prove integration/cancellation seams (W + D).** Recheck both trees and ongoing integration progress, record relevant diffs/SDK versions and preserve user settings/profile changes. Read relevant SDK/extension, session-format, provider, subprocess and Desktop architecture docs/examples in full before implementation. Produce an owned-operation matrix for native shells, nested calls/codemode, explorer/reviewer, MCP/extension tools, provider requests/retries, compaction, verification, IPC/storage, launch/readiness/start acknowledgments and quiescence. For each, identify activity signals, deadline owner, cancellation capability, completion proof and unsupported fallback. Establish actual SDK boundary/UI-wait behavior and generic source-bound host controls with hermetic real-SDK fixtures. Where per-tool cancellation or trustworthy structured outcome metadata is unavailable, use a supported SDK source/dependency seam or explicitly use whole-turn cancellation + fenced unknown ownership; do not assume `tool_call` can replace the execution signal. Revalidate D's reported contracts in its own repository before editing; the independent review could not access that tree. **Acceptance:** an explicit capability/dependency table; unsupported safety-critical supervision blocks autonomous dispatch rather than advertising a complete feature.","sourceLines":{"start":144,"end":144},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-2","label":"2","text":"**Define recovery contracts, configuration and precedence (W; mirrored generic D wire only).** Add focused typed modules for failure facts, cancellation provenance, recovery episodes, operational counters and finite watchdog policy. Separate command identity, operation identity, request identity and parent task identity. Extend trusted global/project resolution and inherited child limits using `shell-guard-config.ts`'s sparse merge/provenance and strict-write patterns, without rewriting unrelated settings. Add user commands/help/provenance for recovery/watchdog configuration using existing command conventions; retain `/shell-guard limits` compatibility. Validate finite bounds and relationships, hard caps and zero-disabled intervention policy. Define registered long-operation exceptions, ordinary-vs-managed budget ownership and review-round-vs-operation duration. Encode the derived task-progress window, recovery episode end and capped backoff above; neither operation starts nor new recovery sessions reset their elapsed budgets. Specify which novel runtime evidence clears consecutive no-progress and when an ineffective recovery cycle increments the existing limit, without charging the first two shell failures as two exhausted cycles. **Tests:** malformed/untrusted settings, sparse merges, settings parse-failure preservation, child cannot widen, model cannot reset/configure limits, defaults, cross-field repair, and finite progress/episode bounds even with continuously successful repeated reads.","sourceLines":{"start":146,"end":146},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-3","label":"3","text":"**Replace the pure global stop latch with command quarantine (W).** Refactor `shell-guard.ts` to maintain per-command executed-timeout counts and separate validation/refusal history, plus a strategy-change decision instead of `action:'stop'`. Use complete-byte opaque hashing with canonical cwd/tool identity and bounded storage that does not evict an active quarantine or unknown in-flight call into an allowed state. Correct failure totals/history and define success/reset behavior explicitly. Reserve same-command execution slots for batches. Two different failures must leave safe alternatives available; third identical execution after two timeouts must never launch. **Tests:** two same vs two different commands, refusal vs executed timeout, quote/whitespace semantics, >2000-character commands, changed timeout/tool aliases, different cwd, successful unrelated commands, duplicate call IDs, batch reservations, resource limits and conservative overflow.","sourceLines":{"start":148,"end":148},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-4","label":"4","text":"**Fix runtime failure delivery without aborting the request (W).** Update `shell-guard-runtime.ts`, `index.ts` hooks and status wording. Remove request-abort/manual-new-prompt behavior from command-limit handling; return honest error guidance from both pre-launch refusal and finalized execution paths. Normalize native timeout provenance, track actual execution start/end, capture partial artifacts safely and avoid double counting `tool_result` plus `tool_execution_end`, including nested calls. Preserve redaction/result metadata and structured-content semantics. Use current session/epoch context rather than a stale first-call closure. **Tests:** second timeout causes zero whole-agent aborts; unrelated permitted tool/command still runs; repeated quarantined command is blocked before execution; ordinary test errors/user aborts are not timeouts; partial output remains; synthetic timeout-like stdout is not authoritative; end-only results and parallel/nested finalization are idempotent.","sourceLines":{"start":150,"end":150},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-5","label":"5","text":"**Add a bounded local continuation at the supported SDK boundary (W).** Implement one request-scoped recovery coordinator connected to `agent_before_settle`, not an `agent_end` loop. On completed outcomes with a newly unresolved recoverable episode and no pending natural continuation/report/user wait, append one transparent instruction with `continue:true`. Persist consumption/correlation before scheduling; preserve other extensions' boundary proposals. Consume/resolve the episode on actual alternate work, explicit blocked report or exhausted recovery. Managed sessions consult the parent-authorized recovery grant and share the same ledger. **Tests:** deterministic provider produces two failures, attempts a premature final reply, receives exactly one continuation and succeeds with a different tool; natural tool continuation adds no duplicate request; subsequent normal completion stays idle; Escape/error/Pause/question/candidate/final blocked result do not restart; races with queued user prompts and other boundary handlers coalesce safely.","sourceLines":{"start":152,"end":152},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-6","label":"6","text":"**Apply shared behavior to explorer and reviewer paths (W).** Update `review-tools.ts`, `review-runtime.ts` and explorer child setup to use the new failure/quarantine contract, removing shell-trip-driven reviewer abort. Preserve verdict submission, pass completion, review pause/error recovery and role permissions. Add finite outer execution/cancellation/drain limits to `runSingleAgent()` and review exploration; supervise exact owned process trees, bound buffered stdout/stderr/JSON framing, finalize once on close/error/timeout and report empty/error outcomes honestly. Parent bounds propagate as ceilings and subprocess cancellation never kills unrelated work. Do not turn read-only explorer into a mutable/headless Builder. **Tests:** native shell failures then alternative inspection for each role, review submission survives the second timeout, truly stalled subagent/provider exits with a clear reason within its outer bound, inherited limits, abort cleanup/escalation, repeated close/error and deliberately unlimited review round with individually bounded operations.","sourceLines":{"start":154,"end":154},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-7","label":"7","text":"**Make request/task recovery durable and migration-safe (W).** Restore command quarantine, recovery episodes, intents/acks and counters through SDK-owned entries for ordinary sessions and the run journal for managed tasks. Use the journal as authority and worker entries as correlated references/projections, not competing writable copies. Persist remaining no-progress/episode active-time budgets and evidence references as well as counts; reload cannot grant a new full window. Compaction/model change/automatic continuation/reopen/rollover cannot reset managed budgets. A genuinely new ordinary user request establishes a fresh scope; steering does not. Quarantine/recovery reset commands require real idle and explicit user intent; managed task total budget increases require a journaled authorized action. Legacy stop entries are history, not permanent active latches or instructions to auto-resume old tasks. Unknown schema/corrupt active records fail closed and remain inspectable. **Tests:** reload/resume/tree/fork isolation, old stopped sessions stay idle until authorized, scope reconciliation, journal failure before effect, torn tail, budget bypass by new session/task ID and bounded retention without replay holes.","sourceLines":{"start":156,"end":156},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-8","label":"8","text":"**Instrument real runtime activity and expected waits (W + generic SDK/D seams).** Add a session-owned activity tracker driven by actual request/stream, tool prepare/start/update/end, nested-call, queue, retry, compaction, UI-prompt and settle events. Maintain operation IDs, monotonic start/deadline, last activity, last useful progress, pending tool/queue counts, stop origin and nested wait stack. Do not infer business progress from tokens or output. Define bounded evidence identities from trusted resource/revision, normalized inspected range/check target and redacted-result digest or existing checkpoint/check receipt; repeated evidence does not reset progress merely because its call ID changed. Keep raw content out of passive snapshots. Track pre-execution gate waits separately from actual tool execution and handle custom questionnaires through documented UI-wait signals. Use outer-wait accounting where the SDK coalesces prompts; obtain a supported seam if true inner nesting is needed. Suspend only clocks actually blocked on that human wait, not unrelated concurrent execution. Publish bounded snapshots/heartbeats independent of model calls; no slow I/O in streaming handlers. **Tests:** silent but healthy long reasoning, active tool without stdout, continuous meaningless output, new read-only evidence vs identical repeated reads, nested human waits inside tools, a human prompt parallel to an overdue shell, tool validation refusal, SDK retries/compaction, mixed parallel tools and follow-ups; missing signals yield unknown, never false idle/quiescence.","sourceLines":{"start":158,"end":158},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-9","label":"9","text":"**Correct and extend generic Desktop inspection/control (D + W adapter).** Version/negotiate a bounded generic session-health snapshot in W `session-host.ts` and D `src/shared/related-sessions.ts`, implemented through D's related-session host/main paths and `session-service.ts`. Include actual session/host epoch, sequence/observation time, idle/busy/settled state, active operation/deadline, queues, expected wait and last typed failure/stop origin. Implement it from `sessionSnapshot`/event tracking, not `tab.status`. Preserve actual fields in W `orchestrator-desktop-host.ts`'s `resultFrom()`/`inspect()`. Give every new logical inspect, interrupt, open, focus and close a fresh request ID; reuse an ID only to retry that same operation against the same target epoch. Keep create/launch dedupe tied to its existing logical intent. Scope receipt caches to operation/target/epoch and invalidate on teardown/rebind; a prior open/close/focus success cannot satisfy a later distinct action. Do not cache health as a durable command receipt or synthesize `running:false` when fields are absent. Implement/reuse the unfinished `host-bridge-auth.ts` host-issued source-bound capability contract for privileged status/control; command-name lookup alone is insufficient. Production issuers must inject a platform CSPRNG (for example Node `crypto.randomBytes` behind the host port), with at least 128 bits of entropy and bounded collision refusal/retry; do not retain the helper's `Math.random()` fallback as a production capability source. Keep deterministic random injection for tests only. Keep SDK access in `src/host/sdk/*` and platform effects behind injected ports. **Tests:** changing running→idle→running inspection through both adapters, stale and late snapshots, missing fields/version support, repeated interrupts as distinct operations, reopen→close→reopen and repeated focus within the 60s cache TTL, same-request retry still idempotent, old-epoch cache refusal, cross-parent/owner/epoch refusal, real-command impersonation, production secure-random wiring and collision handling, teardown and two unrelated extension fixtures.","sourceLines":{"start":160,"end":160},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-10","label":"10","text":"**Wire authenticated terminal and Desktop health/control transport (W + D).** Extend the existing IPC envelope/outbox with validated health snapshots/probes and correlated recovery intent/ack/completion receipts, using actual run/task/attempt/session/start/lease/epoch identity. Supply real local pipe/socket or existing generic Desktop transport effects; capability tokens/secrets never reach prompts/argv/logs. Separate recoverable disconnect from worker death, reject stale/reordered/replayed events, use receiver-local heartbeat freshness and bound buffers/timeouts/reconnect/backoff. A sent request, delivery acknowledgment and actual started/settled action are distinct. **Tests:** process-to-process heartbeat/probe, lost messages/acks, reconnect, duplicate recovery delivery after reload, malformed/oversized payloads, stale lease/attempt, current lease checks on health actions, and explicit unsupported hosts without a hidden fallback.","sourceLines":{"start":162,"end":162},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-11","label":"11","text":"**Extend durable reducers for health/recovery without bypassing acceptance (W).** Integrate typed health/recovering/quiescing/blocked facts and operational recovery counters into `orchestrator-types.ts`, `orchestrator-state.ts`, `orchestrator-store.ts`, `orchestrator-lifecycle.ts`, `orchestrator-repair.ts` and `orchestrator-recovery.ts` using the existing single reducer/journal authority. Prefer a separate operational-health substate where task execution state need not change. Add legal explicit transitions for a running worker that settles without candidate, stalls or crashes; same-attempt recovery must not require inventing a candidate/verification failure. Journal current recovery owner/id, deadline, intent, ack, outcome, user stop origin and cumulative limits. Include task-no-progress window/cycle transitions without turning each successful repeated read into a fresh task. Acceptance/final completion remain dependent on current fenced candidate and real parent evidence. **Tests:** reducer transitions/replay, recovery from silent idle, no candidate-to-accepted shortcut, stale revision/generation, counter charging exactly once, repairs/rollovers cannot reset operational budgets, accepted evidence unchanged and unknown versions rejected.","sourceLines":{"start":164,"end":164},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-12","label":"12","text":"**Implement the passive, phase-aware watchdog (W).** Add a pure diagnosis engine plus a nonblocking runtime timer with injected clocks. Classify healthy, waiting_user, paused/stopped, awaiting_authorization, unexpectedly_idle, overdue_tool, provider_stall, retry/compaction_stall, task_no_progress, disconnected, crashed and ownership_unknown from fresh evidence. Missing heartbeat triggers bounded probe; live heartbeats do not conceal an overdue operation. Evaluate the finite task-progress window independently of operation activity: repeated completed reads/checks with no novel evidence eventually diagnose `task_no_progress`. At expiry reconcile and act at the next safe operation boundary, allowing a healthy in-deadline operation to finish and supply evidence; never reset the window just for a new operation/call ID. If a boundary never arrives, use that operation's own bound and the cancellation ladder. Apply known deadlines before generic limits; preserve remaining budgets across relevant nested waits. Use separate activity/progress clocks and account for host sleep/timer discontinuities. Every non-human wait has a deadline and a concrete next transition; no polling the LLM. **Tests:** table-driven diagnoses for every phase, provider first byte/stream gaps, hidden reasoning, chatty infinite tool, silent legitimate command inside its limit, stale heartbeat with responsive probe, fresh heartbeat with frozen task, indefinitely repeated fast successful reads, novel read-only evidence resetting only consecutive no-progress, nested/parallel waits, timer jumps/suspend and one diagnosis per episode.","sourceLines":{"start":166,"end":166},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-13","label":"13","text":"**Implement bounded interruption and quiescence escalation (W + generic D controls).** Add a reason-tagged cancellation flow: prevent new mutation → cancel exact owned operation/turn → await actual tool/follow-up/process drain with 15s grace → supported owned-process escalation or ownership_unknown. Avoid awaiting idle/abort from inside the same executing tool or event callback. An interrupt RPC success or expired timer never releases the lease. Re-probe before generation changes; PID reuse/foreign process/unknown external effects block replacement. Keep read-only inspection and parent controls responsive while quiescence is unconfirmed. **Tests:** cancel-aware tool, stubborn/ignoring-signal child, dead event loop, late tool result, queued follow-up, process dies after probe, abort command succeeds but run remains busy, and no second writer after grace expiry. No automatic rollback.","sourceLines":{"start":168,"end":168},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-14","label":"14","text":"**Implement reason-directed recovery planning and execution (W).** Build deterministic decisions from diagnosed facts and current approval/budget/ownership, with model-generated alternative strategy only where appropriate. Handle command quarantine/unexpected idle with scoped continuation; task no-progress with a bounded change-strategy cycle at a safe boundary (or owned cancellation/drain first if necessary); transient provider failure with one bounded retry after SDK retry settlement; recoverable transport loss with probe/reattach; exhausted context with existing rollover; confirmed crash with same-session reopen or a visible continuation. Include original objective, observed failure, quarantined attempts, useful progress, partial effects and exact prohibitions in a bounded directive. Persist intent/count before delivery and reconcile uncertain results. Charge ineffective operational cycles once, enforcing the earlier of no-progress, intervention and episode wall-time limits. Unknown credentials/permissions/scope/manual dependency or uncertain external effects surface blocked rather than being disguised as code repair. **Tests:** each classification and ladder edge, recovery uses different approach, configured provider fallback only, same failure repeated exhausts bounds, useful read-only progress recognized, no reset through replacement, no blind mutation replay, and exhausted recovery still leaves actionable status.","sourceLines":{"start":170,"end":170},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-15","label":"15","text":"**Compose live Terminal parent/worker supervision (W).** Integrate with the current worker composition or create the focused missing `orchestrator-runtime` composition layer, keeping `index.ts` thin. Reuse/complete production durable journal/artifacts, cross-process canonical-workspace lease authority, authenticated transport and normal visible interactive terminal session hosting. Use real SDK-managed session IDs/files/bootstrap; acknowledged readiness alone is not mutation authority. Bind activity/failure/control listeners before ready, require current parent start/lease authorization, then one correlated wake and actual start acknowledgment. Connect report/TODO/fence/parent verification and health ticks to that same live runtime. Complete any missing prerequisite from the concurrent integration rather than treating pure modules as production. **Acceptance tests:** actual registered Orchestrator dispatch returns promptly; a real deterministic Builder performs two timed-out commands, uses an alternative without user input, produces a fenced report and reaches real verification; an idle/stalled Builder is diagnosed and recovered or visibly blocked. No parallel writer/headless Builder/assignment replay, and no child before explicit execution approval.","sourceLines":{"start":172,"end":172},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-16","label":"16","text":"**Compose live Desktop supervision and coordinate host ownership (D + W).** Bind the same Workflow recovery policy to normal Desktop-created/resumed child sessions through generic health/control capabilities. Desktop creates/owns one session; W never appends through a second live session manager. Integrate generic supervisor crash/restart/parking events so only one component performs a host restart, while Workflow authorizes task continuation after fresh health/lease/receipt reconciliation. Do not mistake a parked host for a failed task or auto-start a transcript merely on reopen. Respect deliberate tab closure and unknown-close provenance. **Tests:** normal child with real resources/profile/trust/bootstrap, host crash and ready/resumed ordering, parking/wake, duplicate host restart requests, dead host vs healthy idle agent, current session identity after reopen, user-close no recreation and no Workflow-specific branches in Desktop renderer/main.","sourceLines":{"start":174,"end":174},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-17","label":"17","text":"**Connect event-pump delivery and parent recovery ownership (W).** Extend the pump with bounded operational failure/recovery transitions while retaining passive heartbeat/progress. Persist and coalesce recovery wakes, drain only at actual parent safe boundaries, and ensure delivery results in one real parent turn when model judgment is needed. Deterministic permitted probes/cancellation may run in the engine without waking the model. Parent and worker local continuation claim the same episode with revision/CAS fencing; a pending local continuation or candidate suppresses redundant parent continuation. Invalidate callbacks on runtime epoch/disposal and bound the pending queue. **Tests:** parent busy/tools/follow-ups, candidate races watchdog, local before-settle races parent idle recovery, replay after restart, duplicate transport messages, no model turns for heartbeat/progress, and no held parent tool waiting for the child's entire lifetime.","sourceLines":{"start":176,"end":176},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-18","label":"18","text":"**Bound all engine awaits and verification operations (W + D where generic).** Audit the matrix from step 1 against production code: launch/ready/start ack, journal/lease/transport/probe, report/drain/fence, parent/child request, explorer/MCP, retry/compaction, check executor, acceptance and final integration gate. Add operation-aware finite deadlines and cancellation/uncertainty outcomes rather than bare `Promise.race` that leaves a writer unowned. Avoid synchronous unbounded I/O in supervision hot paths; isolate unsafe effects if supported. Parent verification uses normal policy-bound `ctx.executeTool` from a tool context or the existing approved executor, with shell deadlines and truthful timeout evidence. A timed-out/cancelled/skipped check cannot pass acceptance. **Tests:** never-resolving fake port for every phase, hung verify/final check, report arrives while drain stalls, lost start ack, nested tool ignores cancellation, storage failure before recovery intent, and every timeout either safely recovers or reaches a responsive blocked state within its bound.","sourceLines":{"start":178,"end":178},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-19","label":"19","text":"**Integrate explicit operator intent and stall-safe controls (W + D).** Update Pause/Resume/Stop/Retry/Say/Inspect/mode-exit flows to cancel pending automatic recovery, record actor/cause and preserve edits. A busy Stop/Pause must transition to bounded quiescing, then paused/interrupted or an ownership-unknown blocked state—not silently wait forever for a fence. Resume/retry revalidates scope, lease, actual current runtime and remaining budgets; it does not erase command quarantine or assume approval for changed scope. User Escape/Close cancels scheduled wake timers and never causes an automatic continuation. **Tests:** Stop vs timeout, Escape during local boundary, user closes during restart, permission denial vs recovery, input/mode races, stale controls, Review-owned turns and repeated resume/cancel.","sourceLines":{"start":180,"end":180},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-20","label":"20","text":"**Make reload, crash, sleep and parent-loss reconciliation health-aware (W + D).** Fix persisted-running short circuits and file-exists-is-live assumptions. Require fresh probe/process identity/epoch/receipts for recovery; stale/unprobed/foreign child health cannot return healthy resume. Reconstruct remaining budgets/intents conservatively after restart, including elapsed task-progress/recovery windows rather than only counters; rebase live monotonic clocks and re-probe after sleep/network/host changes. Missing ack is uncertain, never a blind resend. Parent loss prevents child mutation at safe gates; new parent ownership waits for previous writer reconciliation. Dispose/unsubscribe timers and pending probes/wakes on session branch/tree/shutdown. **Tests:** crash before/after recovery intent, delivery/ack/settle, lease renewal, cold/warm resume, corrupt/torn journal, PID reuse, suspend with pending human wait, fork/rewind, stale callbacks, missing session file and unknown old owner.","sourceLines":{"start":182,"end":182},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-21","label":"21","text":"**Publish transparent status and diagnostics without model polling (W + generic D UI).** Extend `/shell-guard status`, Orchestrator status and generic contribution rows with actual activity, operation age/deadline, last observation/failure provenance, waiting reason, quarantine/recovery counts, current recovery action/next deadline and clear paused/blocked controls. Make healthy-running, suspected stall, recovering, waiting-user and unconfirmed ownership visually distinct. Expose last supported useful-progress age and the effective no-progress/episode deadline separately from last activity. Emit one concise user notice per meaningful transition, not every heartbeat. Keep bounded durable recovery timelines/artifact links with redaction and retention; omit raw commands/output and secrets from passive exports. **Tests:** both hosts, repeated heartbeat silence, exact failure cause vs unknown wording, changing inspection status, stale UI epoch, unrelated extension fixture, no misleading cancellation/success/rollback claims and no sensitive-output leakage.","sourceLines":{"start":184,"end":184},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-22","label":"22","text":"**Add real-SDK automatic-continuation regression suites (W).** Boot the actual extension and registered tools with temporary agent dirs, deterministic scripted providers and real SDK session managers—beyond fake event emission. Exercise ordinary Default/Plan/Build, managed Builder, explorer and isolated reviewer. The central regression is two actual short native timeouts → second failure visible to model → third identical command refused → different permitted tool/command succeeds → normal final completion, with no user prompt and no guard-wide abort. Also test model premature stop, natural continuation coalescing, local/parent recovery race, ordinary test failure, provider error, redaction, nested tools, explicit human wait and user abort. Include all new suites in the explicit package test script; never consume real user credentials.","sourceLines":{"start":186,"end":186},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-23","label":"23","text":"**Add real-process and Desktop end-to-end fault injection (W + D).** Use harmless owned subprocess fixtures plus real journal/IPC and generic Desktop session adapters. Cover silent/chattering shell hangs, inherited pipes, child ignores cancellation, process/event-loop crash, lost heartbeat with live parent, transport partition, start/recovery lost acknowledgments, provider stream stall, hung MCP/explore/verification, unexpected idle with and without report, a task-progress loop of fast successful repeated reads, parent busy and crash/reload during each recovery phase. Assert bounded detection/action, precise observations, exactly-once receipt/counting, current generation, no second writer, preserved edits, no false acceptance and zero resurrection after user Stop/Close. Exercise Desktop's actual child health snapshot through W, not just isolated bridge validation. Also exercise distinct open/focus/close actions within the receipt TTL across reopen, while preserving retries of the same logical action. Use independent outer test timeouts and verify no fixture process/timer/listener leaks.","sourceLines":{"start":188,"end":188},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-24","label":"24","text":"**Update docs/package contracts and run all automated gates (W + D).** Replace current “one changed approach then stop” help/README/status claims with command quarantine, model-visible continuation and bounded safe recovery. Document defaults/configuration, phase/reason/action table, task-progress evidence/window and recovery-episode/backoff policy, deliberate human waits/Stop/Close, unlimited-review-round distinction, unknown cancellation/ownership, compatibility requirements and recovery-budget exhaustion. Update operations/live-acceptance/release-readiness docs and Unreleased changelog; add all runtime modules to W's explicit package files/test lists. Run changed-path active LSP plus confirmed typechecks, focused/full suites, policy/architecture gates and packed-package load verification. Review final diffs against the captured concurrent baseline. No publish/version bump/tag/push or broad user configuration rewrite is authorized.","sourceLines":{"start":190,"end":190},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false},{"roadmapStepId":"rm-25","label":"25","text":"**Perform and record live acceptance before claiming readiness (Terminal + packaged Desktop).** With the completed baseline integration, run the acceptance matrix below in visible Windows Terminal and packaged Desktop with a real provider. Verify ordinary-session automatic alternative and Orchestrator recovery through candidate verification/next-task progression, not just launch/status text. Test permission/question waits, Stop/Escape/Close and actual crash/reopen. Run macOS/Linux adapter signoff separately before claiming platform parity. Record exact versions, timings, outcomes, costs where known and remaining blockers. Any provider/platform/manual test not performed stays **NOT RUN**; inability to prove cancellation/single-writer safety blocks autonomous rollout rather than being marked complete.","sourceLines":{"start":192,"end":192},"phasePath":[],"claimedComplete":false,"completionVerified":false}],"phases":[],"lineCount":280,"createdAt":1795329505214}